            "body": {
                "serial": "container_containeritembody_5ed4ca739554c292044072",
                "body": "<div class=\"grid-row\">  <div class=\"col-6\"><div class=\"custom-text-box\" data-scrolling=\"false\"><p>Read the following passage:</p><div class=\"custom-include-box key-navigation-focusable tao-overflow-y tao-half-height\" data-scrolling=\"true\" data-scrolling-height=\"50\">{{xinclude_5ed4ca7395879552200821}}</div></div></div>  <div class=\"col-6\"><div class=\"custom-text-box\" data-scrolling=\"false\"><p>Read the following passage:</p><div class=\"custom-include-box key-navigation-focusable tao-overflow-y tao-half-height\" data-scrolling=\"true\" data-scrolling-height=\"50\">{{xinclude_5ed4ca7395879552200822}}</div></div></div>  </div> <div class=\"grid-row\"><div class=\"col-12\"><p>Literary criticism (or literary studies) is the study, evaluation, and interpretation of literature. Modern literary criticism is often influenced by literary theory, which is the philosophical discussion of literature's goals and methods. Though the two activities are closely related, literary critics are not always, and have not always been, theorists.</p></div></div> <div class=\"grid-row\">  <div class=\"col-8\">{{interaction_choiceinteraction_5ed4ca7395689041975837}}</div>  <div class=\"col-4\"><p>Later in the exam you will be prompted for a deeper analysis of these texts.</p></div>  </div>",
